# Build-time ignore list for `license_manager/Dockerfile.render`.
#
# Docker reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` from the Dockerfile's own directory,
# and patterns are matched against the build context — which is `new_app/`
# (the API needs `backend/`, the dashboard needs `license_manager/dashboard/`).
#
# This is an exclusion list, not an allowlist: the Dockerfile copies only the
# paths it needs. The rules below keep credentials, host build output, tests and
# unrelated POS artifacts out of the context entirely, so they cannot be copied
# by accident and the context stays small on Render's builder.

**/.git
**/.git/**
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/tests
**/logs
**/backups
**/data
**/.DS_Store
**/appsettings*.json
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Credentials and key material: never part of any image.
**/application_default_credentials.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/*-key*.json
**/LICENSE_API_CODE_ENC_SECRET
**/LICENSE_API_SIGNING_SECRET
**/*.pem

# Staging does not carry the PRODUCTION verification keys or release record.
# (They are public material, but nothing in this image may reference them.)
backend/app/licensing/verification_keys.json
backend/app/licensing/release_metadata.json

# Unrelated POS application sources and their build outputs.
lib/
windows/
test/
installer/
docs/

# Documentation and local tooling noise.
**/*.md
**/.DS_Store
